.env
# The whole family, not just `.env`. `.env.local` was covered and a `.env.local.bak-…`, a
# `.env.production` or a `.env.local.old` was not — and this repository is public, so an ignore
# pattern that covers only the exact name is one careless `cp` away from publishing a credential.
# `.env.example` is the one that is meant to be tracked, so it is excepted rather than the rule
# being loosened.
.env.*
!.env.example

